  "query_preview": "..\nA broad upper trough over the Gulf of Alaska will allow storm\nsystems to crash into British Columbia over the next several days\nwith drier/weaker systems emerging over Alberta and Sask.\n\nThis will bring some instances of winds for northeast Montana while\ntemperatures are expected to remain above normal. The first weak \nfront will move in late tonight/Saturday. A wind gust to 58 mph \nhas a low confidence (30-50%) of occurring but issued a High Wind \nWarning to cover.\n\nAlso issued a Lake Wind Advisory for Fort Peck Lake tomorrow from\n7 am till 4 pm as wind gusts of 30-35 mph look to occur.\n\nAnother weak front moves in late Sunday for an uptick in winds,\nbut not as strong.\n\nRidging aloft builds back in for most of next week, although low\nlevel easterly winds could inhibit full warming potential.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nSlight edits to Wind Gusts late tonight and Saturday with a blend\nto NBM90. TFJ",
